# Redoubt isolation-media-process.patch  (Android, android.txt, 158.0-2)
# Owner: LW-M7-50 (isolated content with H.264/AAC via RDD); docs/android/ISOLATION-MEDIA.md
#
# Owner decisions, verbatim:
#   2026-10-10 plan        "Prototype now, ship ON in a 158 dot release if it tests clean"
#   2026-10-10 trade-off   "Keep software codecs in the page process"
#   2026-10-11 rollout     "158.0-2, Android 12+ only"
#
# Upstream file touched
# ---------------------
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/gecko/GeckoProvider.kt
#
# THE runtime gate. The two literals isolated-process.patch (LW-M5-02, revised
# by LW-M7-43) pins to false become one value, GeckoProvider.isolatedContentEnabled():
# Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 31 (Android 12). On Android 12+ content runs in
# `zygoteTab` services, as u:r:isolated_app with its own isolated uid, forked
# from the app zygote, and cannot read the profile directory. On Android 8-11
# both stay false and content runs as in 158.0-1 (untrusted_app, app uid).
# Still not read from Settings or Nimbus: only the OS version decides, so no
# experiment and no settings write can move it (isolated-process.patch, "Why the
# value is hard-coded").
#
# Why Android 12+ only: on the API 30 emulator (OMX codec stack) 9 of 17 media
# runs were flaky with upstream's eleven isolated-process prefs, including on
# builds without any Redoubt code (docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-50/README.md
# section 5); API 34 (Codec2) and the owner's Pixel 10 Pro (Android 17) are clean.
# Android 8-11 keep today's behaviour until that flake is understood.
#
# Everything else follows THIS value, so the media configuration cannot
# disagree with the process model: GeckoView reads the effective content process
# type from its process manager and passes media.redoubt-isolation-media.enabled
# to Gecko, which then sets and locks upstream's eleven isolated-process media
# prefs (isolation-media-prefs.patch) and turns the codec allowlist on
# (isolation-media-codecs-in-content.patch). Below Android 12 the gate is
# false and none of that happens.
#
# Native HLS, decided: FAIL CLOSED under isolation, no workaround.
# HLSDecoder::IsEnabled() is `media_hls_enabled() &&
# !GeckoAppShell::IsIsolatedProcess()` (dom/media/hls/HLSDecoder.cpp:360-363
# in 158.0), because the ExoPlayer-based GeckoHlsPlayer cannot bind services
# from an isolated process (bug 2043165). So on Android 12+
# canPlayType("application/vnd.apple.mpegurl") is "" and a page whose ONLY
# source is a native <video src=".m3u8"> gets MEDIA_ERR_SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED
# (error 4); pages that feature-detect (hls.js, video.js, Shaka, every major
# player) fall back to MSE, which plays H.264/AAC through RDD. Android 8-11
# keep native HLS.
#
# Ordering: must apply AFTER patches/android/isolated-process.patch (its context
# is that patch's comment block and literals); declared in
# scripts/check-patch-order.py. Listed at the end of assets/patches/android.txt.
#
--- a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/gecko/GeckoProvider.kt
+++ b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/gecko/GeckoProvider.kt
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
